.TH RPMDB2SUMMARY 1 "Nov 5, 2026" "" ""
.SH NAME
.B rpmdb2summary
prints rpmdb(8) content in pkg_summary(5) format.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.BI rpmdb2summary " -a|-A|-u [OPTIONS] [packages...]"
.br
.BI rpmdb2summary "          [OPTIONS] [packages...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rpmdb2summary
reads rpmdb(8) content on rpm-based system and print information
about packages in pkg_summary(5) format.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "-h"
Display help message.
.TP
.B "-A"
Output information about all installed packages.
.TP
.B "-a"
Output information about auto-installed packages.
.TP
.B "-u"
Output information about user-installed packages.
.TP
.B "-p"
Use package file names instead of rpmdb (option -p is passed to
.BR rpm(1) ).
.TP
.B "-r"
Use field names from
.BR "rpm -qi" .
.TP
.BI "-f " "format"
Output summary in specified form.
.SH EXAMPLES
.VB
   rpmdb2summary -ru
   rpmdb2summary gawk bmake
   rpmdb2summary -f 'Name=%{nevr}\\n[Filename=%{filenames}\\n]' gawk bmake
.VE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkg_summary(5) ,
.BR rpm(1) ,
